The '''VCX-100 light freighter''' was one of the [[Corellian Engineering Corporation]]'s [[freighter]] designs. A notable example of this model was the ''[[Ghost]]'', a modified VCX-100 owned by [[Hera Syndulla]].

==Characteristics==
[[File:Hera_Syndulla_VCX-100_XWM.png|thumb|left|250px|The ''Ghost'' firing its dorsal turret at an Imperial cruiser]]
The VCX-100 was outfitted with sleeping quarters, a galley, and a common room. Its armament comprised a dorsal [[turret]] and a forward-mounted chin turret, the latter being controlled by a [[gunner]] in its seat or from the cockpit. The cargo bay and main entrance ramp of the VCX-100 were mostly located in the front of the [[freighter]], below the forward-turret. VCX-100s also had a slot in between its main [[engine]]s, into which a [[VCX-series auxiliary starfighter]] could dock. The VCX-100 was also outfitted with a magnetic cargo clamp on its ventral plating, capable of holding several bulk containers.<ref name="Visual Guide" />

==History==
{{Quote|Sir, comscan has identified the Corellian VCX as the supply transport.|An Imperial officer to ISB Agent Alexsandr Kallus, during the [[Blockade of Ibaar|blockade]] of [[Ibaar]]|<ref name="Wings of the Master">{{Rebels|Wings of the Master}}</ref>}}
In [[10 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> before [[Han Solo]] owned the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'', Solo played a game of [[Sabacc]] against [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] to try to win the latter's starship. Solo bluffed that he owned a VCX-100 to use as collateral in order to get Calrissian's attention.<ref name="Solo" />

[[File:Ghost.png|thumb|left|250px|The ''Ghost'' flown by Hera Syndulla]]
In [[5 BBY]], a VCX-100 light freighter was docked at a ship yard on [[Ferrix]].<ref name="Kassa">{{Andor|Kassa (episode)}}</ref>

The ''Ghost'' was a notable VCX-100, piloted by [[Hera Syndulla]].<ref name="MitG">{{Rebels|The Machine in the Ghost}}</ref> In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> the ''Ghost'' participated in the [[Battle of Scarif]]<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> and the [[Battle of Endor]]<ref name="An Imperial Feast">{{FOD|An Imperial Feast}}</ref> in [[4 ABY]].<ref name="Timelines" />

In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> at least three VCX-100 light freighters including the ''Ghost'' were part of a [[Citizens' Fleet|fleet]] assembled by [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] to assist the Resistance during the [[Battle of Exegol|battle]] against the [[Sith Eternal military|Sith Eternal forces]] over the [[planet]] [[Exegol]].<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

